# The root and the boot image's modules (roadmap l4.md L5): through the
# capabilities the kernel gave it, the root finds each module's code where
# the module table says, and its code and data as assembled (Fletcher sums
# of what it reads, against the image's). The drivers' code, of ring 1, is
# not the root's to read: "----".
program: shell
define: TEST_ROOT_REPORT
---
rx286, test build
root: module os: code at {m:os.base}h, sum {m:os.codesum}, data sum {m:os.datasum}
root: module printer: code at {m:printer.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:printer.datasum}
root: module mouse: code at {m:mouse.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:mouse.datasum}
root: module console: code at {m:console.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:console.datasum}
root: module kbd: code at {m:kbd.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:kbd.datasum}
root: module fd: code at {m:fd.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:fd.datasum}
root: module hd: code at {m:hd.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:hd.datasum}
root: module serial: code at {m:serial.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:serial.datasum}
root: module sound: code at {m:sound.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:sound.datasum}
root: module rtc: code at {m:rtc.base}h, sum ----, data sum {m:rtc.datasum}
root: module program: code at {m:program.base}h, sum {m:program.codesum}, data sum {m:program.datasum}
root: module counter: code at {m:counter.base}h, sum {m:counter.codesum}, data sum {m:counter.datasum}
root: module z: code at {m:z.base}h, sum {m:z.codesum}, data sum {m:z.datasum}
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>
